clean_summary:
We introduce TAPA, a position encoding method that separates magnitude from angular contributions. TAPA achieves better out-of-distribution performance on long-context tasks compared to the vanilla RoPE approach. Theoretical analysis explains why it works.

Thanks to @yusidwang and colleagues for their great work.

@yusidwang: "We’d like to introduce our paper on long-context positional encoding, centered on a simple principle."
